@startsalt
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
' purpose: how sbx's own dashboard, modals and controls look and behave, recorded so proveo can borrow the vocabulary
' status: observed 2026-11-10 on sbx v0.50.0 (30d023c), darwin/arm64; a record, not a contract.
'   what proveo takes from it ...... _spec/_plans/wizard-upgrades.puml
'   the Ctrl+C half ................ _spec/_plans/tui-responsiveness.puml
'   proveo's own resolved layout ... _spec/internal/choiceui/wireframe.puml
'
' ── HOW THIS WAS RECORDED ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
' `sbx tui` ran in a detached tmux pane, 150x50. Each screen was captured twice:
' `tmux capture-pane -p` for the text and `-e -p` for the SGR runs. Colours are
' the 24-bit values sbx emits with TERM=xterm-256color, COLORTERM=truecolor and
' TMUX unset. Inside tmux it downsamples to the 256-colour palette.
' Raw captures are not committed: they hold host names and paths from live
' sandboxes.
' NOT PRESSED, on purpose: `s` (start/stop), `r` (remove), `Enter` (attach) and
' `x` (shell). Three sandboxes held live sessions. The stop and remove
' confirmations are therefore not recorded.
' [Unverified] Whether `s` and `r` ask before acting.
' `a` and `b` (allow / block a host) and `t` (theme) were not pressed either:
' they change policy or a saved setting.
'
' ── THE STACK ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' MEASURED with `go version -m $(command -v sbx)`: charm.land/bubbletea/v2
' v2.0.10, lipgloss/v2 v2.0.6, bubbles/v2 v2.2.1, glamour/v2 v2.0.1,
' charmbracelet/ultraviolet, charmbracelet/colorprofile v0.4.3,
' muesli/cancelreader v0.2.2, spf13/cobra v1.10.2, x/term v0.46.0.
'
' ── THE PALETTE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   #e5f2fc  bold  the app name, the active tab, a key in the footer, a
'                  selected card's name, the mnemonic letter of "exec"
'   #c0c0c0  bold  a modal's question, a selected list item
'   #808080        every description: footer words, inactive tabs, stats, dates
'   #7aa2f7        the focused panel's border, the cursor ▸, the step chip text
'   #5c648f        an unfocused panel's border; #484c5e and darker under a modal
'   #7dcfff  bold  the split bar between panels (on #282d42); "info"
'   #b083ea  bold  a chip: the card's "Sandbox" tag, "All sandboxes ▾" (on #39304a)
'   #e0af68        attention: "stop", a stopped card's ■ and state, the !§ badge
'   #f7768e        destructive or blocked: "remove", "block", "● 0 blocked"
'   #9ece6a        healthy: "● 39 allowed", "Allowed"
'   #282d42  bg    an unselected button, a badge, the step chip
'   #7aa2f7  bg    the SELECTED button, with #000000 bold text
'
' ── THE MNEMONIC LETTER ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' A card's action row reads "stop  exec  remove  info". On the SELECTED card one
' letter per word is bold and bright, and the rest of the word is the same hue
' dimmed:
'   s  bold #e0af68   top    #a17d4a
'   x  bold #e5f2fc   e, ec  #a4aeb5     the letter sits mid-word
'   r  bold #f7768e   emove  #b15466
'   i  bold #7dcfff   nfo    #5995b7
' The bold letter IS the key. On every other card the row is one dim colour
' with no bold letter, so only the card that would act shows keys.
' An inline row action uses the same device: the selected log row carries
' "block" with a bold red b.
' TABS DO NOT USE IT. The active tab is bold #e5f2fc, the others #808080, and
' with the panel unfocused all three are grey. ← and → move between them.
'
' ── THE FOOTER IS CONTEXTUAL ───────────────────────────────────────────────
' One line, bottom-left, version bottom-right. A key is bold #e5f2fc and its
' word is #808080, two spaces between pairs. The pairs change with focus:
'   sandboxes   ^c quit  ↑/↓/←/→/Tab navigate  Enter run  c create  n network
'   network log ^c quit  ↑/↓/←/→/Tab navigate  / search  o status  n network  f filesystem
'   net rules   ^c quit  ↑/↓/←/→/Tab navigate  / search  o type  a add rule  r remove resource  …
'   searching   Esc cancel  Enter apply
'   full screen ^c quit  ↑/↓/←/→/Tab navigate  / search  s sandbox  o status  Esc back
' The same letter means different things by panel: `r` removes a sandbox on the
' left and refreshes data on the right; `s` stops a sandbox on the left and
' opens the sandbox filter on the right.
'
' ── MODALS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' A centred box with a #6b75a8 border, a ✕ top-right, a bold grey title, and a
' rule under it. The dashboard stays drawn behind it with its borders dimmed.
'   exit      Ctrl+C opens it. "No ↵" is selected. ←/→ move the selection and
'             the ↵ glyph follows it. Esc closes. A second Ctrl+C quits, status
'             0. Sandboxes are untouched.
'   create    A stepped wizard. The chip reads 1/2 and becomes 2/3 once "Local"
'             is chosen: the count follows the answers. "Next ↵" sits
'             bottom-right as the selected button. Esc steps BACK one page and
'             closes only from page 1. A list scrolls behind a bar on its right
'             edge.
'   settings  Label left, value right as a badge. "Theme (t)" names its key in
'             the label. One "Close" button.
'   info      Titled sections with a rule drawn to the box edge: Identity,
'             Mounts, Ports, Resources, Network. "↑/↓ scroll  Esc close".
'   help      Ctrl+h or ?. Titled by the view ("Split View — Keyboard
'             Shortcuts"), grouped Global / Navigation / Actions / Mouse, and
'             the groups change with the focused panel.
' A full-screen view (n, f) grows a "❮ esc" cell at the left of the header bar
' and adds "Esc back" to the footer.
' Docs: "At selection and text prompts, Enter accepts the default. Ctrl-D
' cancels the prompt." (docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/usage/)
